@page "/"

<PageTitle>Home</PageTitle>

<h1>Multiple client apps</h1>

<p>
    This page and the login page are static server-side rendered by <code>MultipleClientsWeb</code>:
    no WebAssembly runtime is downloaded here.
</p>

<ul data-enhance-nav="false">
    <li><a href="admin">Admin</a> - the <code>MultipleClientAdmin</code> WebAssembly client (role Admin).</li>
    <li><a href="game">Game</a> - the <code>MultipleClientGame</code> WebAssembly client (any logged in user).</li>
</ul>

<h2>Cache busting</h2>

<p>
    Ways to keep static assets cacheable without serving stale files after a deployment; see the README. The badge
    <VersionBadge /> comes from <code>MultipleClientShared</code>; in the clients it also imports a versioned JS module.
</p>

<table class="table table-sm asset-examples">
    <thead>
        <tr><th>Technique</th><th>Url on this page</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><td>Host file through <code>@@Assets[...]</code>: fingerprinted</td><td><code>@Assets["app.css"]</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Library file through <code>@@Assets[...]</code>: fingerprinted</td><td><code>@Assets[SharedAssets.CssBundle]</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Library file, url built by the library: version query</td><td><code>@SharedAssets.AppendVersion(SharedAssets.Logo)</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Library JS module for <code>import()</code>: version query</td><td><code>@SharedAssets.ModuleUrl(SharedAssets.AssetInfoModule)</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Library scoped CSS <code>@@import</code>: fingerprinted by the SDK</td><td><code>_content/MultipleClientShared/MultipleClientShared.{hash}.bundle.scp.css</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Image <code>url()</code> in library scoped CSS: version query added at build</td><td><code>images/badge-bg.svg?v=@SharedAssets.Version</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Client runtime: fingerprinted through the import map</td><td><code>@Assets["admin-client/_framework/dotnet.js"]</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Another area's file through <code>@@Assets[...]</code>: not in this page's collection, left as is</td><td><code>@Assets["admin-client/images/admin-picture.svg"]</code></td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h2>Pictures through <code>@@Assets[...]</code></h2>

<p>
    The admin and game pages show their own picture next to this shared one, resolved by the same component.
</p>

<AssetPicture Path="@SharedAssets.Picture" Alt="Shared layers" />
